      },
      "text": "### Generalized Hooke's Law (3D)"
    },
    {
      "id": "02-MECHANICS-OF-MATERIALS.md#015",
      "path": [
        "02-MECHANICS-OF-MATERIALS.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:structural:02-mechanics-of-materials, git-history:structural:02-mechanics-of-materials]",
        "canonical_path": "structural/02-MECHANICS-OF-MATERIALS.md",
        "concepts": "[mechanics, of, materials]",
        "current_path": "structural/02-MECHANICS-OF-MATERIALS.md",
        "id": "maxim:structural:mechanics-of-materials",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "structural",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[mechanics, of]",
        "section": "structural",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "02 - Mechanics of Materials",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "The full 3D constitutive relation is sigma = C : epsilon, where C is a 4th-order elasticity tensor (3x3x3x3 = 81 components). Symmetry of stress and strain tensors reduces independent components to 36. Material isotropy collapses 36 to just 2 independent constants (E and nu, or equivalently lambda and mu). This is a linear map from the 6-component Voigt stress vector to the 6-component Voigt strain vector — a 6x6 matrix with only 2 free parameters:"
    },
    {
      "id": "02-MECHANICS-OF-MATERIALS.md#016",
      "path": [
        "02-MECHANICS-OF-MATERIALS.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:structural:02-mechanics-of-materials, git-history:structural:02-mechanics-of-materials]",
        "canonical_path": "structural/02-MECHANICS-OF-MATERIALS.md",
        "concepts": "[mechanics, of, materials]",
        "current_path": "structural/02-MECHANICS-OF-MATERIALS.md",
        "id": "maxim:structural:mechanics-of-materials",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "structural",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[mechanics, of]",
        "section": "structural",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "02 - Mechanics of Materials",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "```\nε_x = (σ_x − ν(σ_y + σ_z)) / E\nε_y = (σ_y − ν(σ_x + σ_z)) / E\nε_z = (σ_z − ν(σ_x + σ_y)) / E\nγ_xy = τ_xy / G    (similarly for xz, yz)\n```"
    },
